WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
Britain today is home
to Christians, Muslims,

2
00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:08.590
Jews, Hindus, Sikhs, Buddhists,
and many people of no religion.

3
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.920
One verse of the Qur'an says there
is no compulsion in religion.

4
00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:18.570
Yet in John's Gospel, Jesus says no one
comes to the Father except through him.

5
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.290
So if you believe your religion is true,
can you also believe other religions

6
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.460
are true?

7
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.780
In this mission, you'll meet
three answers to that question,

8
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.170
drawn as paths up a mountain.

9
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.960
Then you'll test those answers
against what believers really say,

10
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.770
in their own words.

11
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.670
Your mission: weigh up whether believing
in one truth leaves room for others.
